<title>RUSSIA: Russia to sell military helicopters to Slovakia.</title>
<headline>Russia to sell military helicopters to Slovakia.</headline>
<dateline>VLADIVOSTOK 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Arsenyev helicopter manufacturer in the Far East will sell six Ka-50 military helicopters to Slovakia, a company official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;In March we will sign an agreement,&quot; chief engineer Alexander Mironov said, adding that the plant was in the final stage of talks with Slovakian officials.</p>
<p>Mironov did not give the price of an export modification of the Ka-50, but aviation experts estimated the cost at $9-$10.5 million.</p>
<p>The Arsenyev plant also makes the single-seat Ka-50 combat helicopter, known as Black Shark, for the Russian Army.</p>
<p>The plant resumed production on the aircraft only towards the end of last year, after a nearly two-year halt because of financial problems.</p>
<p>--Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow News, + 7095 941 8520</p>
